title: Renames that follow
intro: Renaming an entity now renames it in every field that names it, and a name that matches nothing is flagged.
project: Platformer | Renames

chapter: Rename, and the fields follow | F2 in the Hierarchy
select: Main Camera
explain: field:Follow.Target | Follows the player | The camera follows whatever its Target names. Right now, that's the player.
select: Player
say: Let's give the player a proper name. Press F2 and type it.
key: F2
type: Hero\n
expectvalue: Main Camera.Follow.Target = Hero
expectvalue: Health Bar.Bar.Track = Hero
select: Main Camera
explain: field:Follow.Target | Renamed here too | The camera's Target changed along with it, and so did the health bar's, so nothing loses track of the hero.
say: It's one undo step, too. Undo puts the old name back everywhere at once.

chapter: Its own, or someone else's | Names inside come first
select: Hint
say: The lever and the sign each have a hint called Hint, shown when you walk up to them. Let's rename the lever's.
key: F2
type: Lever Hint\n
expectvalue: Lever.Switch.Prompt = Lever Hint
expectvalue: Sign.Dialogue.Prompt = Hint
select: Lever
explain: field:Switch.Prompt | Its own hint | The lever's Prompt follows its own hint. The sign's still names the sign's, just the way the game finds them.

chapter: Names that match nothing | Flagged in the Inspector
select: Main Camera
set: Follow.Target = Heroo
expectflagged: Follow.Target = Heroo
explain: field:Follow.Target | Nothing by that name | A typo. Nothing in the scene is called that, so the field turns amber with a warning sign, and its tip says which name it can't find.
pickentity: Follow.Target = Hero
expectflagged: Follow.Target = none
say: Pick the right one, and the warning goes away.
select: Bridge
say: Deleting something leaves the fields that named it pointing at nothing.
key: Delete
select: Lever
expectflagged: Switch.Targets = Bridge
explain: field:Switch.Targets | The bridge is gone | The lever still names the bridge, so it's flagged. Undo brings the bridge back, and the warning goes with it.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectflagged: Switch.Targets = none
